message.content:
Create the file `C:\Users\User\comfyui-agent\agent\profiles\flux1-dev.yaml` — the complete Flux.1 Dev model communication profile.

This is the FIRST and most important model profile. It must encode real, specific knowledge about Flux.1 Dev behavior. NOT generic defaults — real model-specific knowledge that took experimentation to learn.

Key Flux.1 Dev characteristics to encode:
- DiT (Diffusion Transformer) architecture, not UNet
- Native 1024x1024 resolution
- Uses FluxGuidance node (guidance_scale), NOT traditional CFG
- T5 text encoder for prompting — natural language style, NOT tag-based
- CFG sweet spot is very low (2.5-4.5), NOT the 7-12 range of SD1.5/SDXL
- Negative prompts have LOW effectiveness (Flux doesn't respond to negatives well)
- Euler and DPM++ 2M are the recommended samplers
- DDIM should be avoided
- 20 steps is the sweet spot, diminishing returns above 35
- Excellent photorealistic skin texture and coherent lighting
- Hands/fingers are the primary failure mode
- Color banding at high CFG (>7)
- Smooth gradients without banding at proper settings
- Supports multiple aspect ratios: 1:1, 16:9, 9:16, 4:3, 3:4
- Token weighting uses parenthetical style
- Max effective tokens ~256

The profile MUST follow this exact structure with all 3 consumer sections:

```yaml
meta:
  model_id: "flux1-dev"
  model_class: "flux"
  base_arch: "dit"
  modality: "image"
  version_hash: ""

prompt_engineering:  # Intent Agent section
  style: "natural_language"
  positive_prompt: { structure, keyword_sensitivity, effective_patterns, token_weighting, max_effective_tokens }
  negative_prompt: { required_base, style, effectiveness }
  intent_translations:  # CRITICAL - map artistic words to parameter directions
    "dreamier": { cfg_direction: lower, sampler_preference, prompt_additions, denoise_direction }
    "sharper": { ... }
    "more stylized": { ... }
    "more photorealistic": { ... }
    "moodier": { ... }
    "more abstract": { ... }
    "warmer": { ... }
    "cooler": { ... }
    "more detailed": { ... }
    "softer": { ... }
    "more dramatic": { ... }
    "more natural": { ... }

parameter_space:  # Execution Agent section
  steps: { default, range, sweet_spot, diminishing_returns }
  cfg: { default, range, sweet_spot, failure_modes }
  sampler: { recommended, avoid, scheduler }
  resolution: { native, supported_ratios, upscale_friendly }
  denoise: { default, img2img_sweet_spot }
  lora_behavior: { max_simultaneous, strength_range, default_strength, interaction_model, known_conflicts }

quality_signatures:  # Verify Agent section
  expected_characteristics: [list of what good Flux output looks like]
  known_artifacts: [list of {condition, artifact} pairs]
  quality_floor: { description, reference_score }
  iteration_signals: { needs_more_steps, needs_lower_cfg, needs_higher_cfg, needs_reprompt, needs_inpaint, model_limitation }
```

Include RICH comments throughout explaining WHY each value is what it is. The intent_translations section should have at least 12 artistic intent entries. The known_artifacts should have at least 5 specific conditions. This profile should encode knowledge that took hours of experimentation to learn.
